"  (a record was removed), `switch_to` (a user took over another\n"
"  user's session via _View from user's perspective_),\n"
"  `switch_back_to` (the original session was resumed).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/audit-log.md:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`auditable_id`\n"
":\n"
"  ID of the record that was changed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/audit-log.md:107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`auditable_type`\n"
": Class name of the record that was changed (e.g. `Macro`,\n"
"  `Setting`, `KnowledgeBase`, `ChecklistTemplate`, `Job`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/audit-log.md:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`auditable_name`\n"
": Display name of the changed record at the time the entry was\n"
"  written. Stored separately so it remains readable after the record\n"
"  itself is gone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/audit-log.md:116
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`value_from`\n"
": Object (JSON) holding the previous state of the audited\n"
"  attributes. Empty (`{}`) on `create` entries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/audit-log.md:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`value_to`\n"
": Object (JSON) holding the new state of the audited attributes.\n"
"  Empty (`{}`) on `destroy` entries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/audit-log.md:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`source_ip`\n"
": IP address that issued the underlying request. `Rails console`\n"
"  or `Rails runner` is stored when the entry was written from a\n"
